## Exception: individually deposited papers

Several papers in this series are deposited on Zenodo **under CC BY 4.0**, which is
more permissive than the default above. Where a page reports such a deposit, the
page shows that record's own licence next to its DOI, and **the deposited record
governs that paper**. A Zenodo licence cannot be narrowed after publication, so
where the two differ, the deposit wins.

This is why some pages in this repository carry both licence strings. That is not
a contradiction: the footer states the licence of the *page as part of the series*,
and the deposit block states the licence of the *paper it reports*. When adding a
page, keep both and keep them labelled.

The authoritative list is the Zenodo community, where each record shows its own
licence:

    https://zenodo.org/communities/principia-orthogona

